(b) All subdivision and/or development proposals shall have public utilities and facilities such as sewer, gas, electrical and water systems located and constructed to minimize flood damage;
(c) All subdivision and/or development proposals shall have adequate drainage provided to reduce exposure to flood hazards, and;
(d) For subdivisions and/or developments greater than 50 lots or five acres, whichever is less, base flood elevation data shall be provided for subdivision and all other proposed development, including manufactured home parks and subdivisions. Any changes or revisions to the flood data adopted herein and shown on the FIRM shall be submitted to FEMA for review as a conditional letter of map revision (CLOMR) or conditional letter of map amendment (CLOMA), whichever is applicable. Upon completion of the project, the developer is responsible for submitting the "as-built" data to FEMA in order to obtain the final LOMR.
(Ord. of 8-2-2010, Art. 4, § F)

258:
(a) A person desiring to obtain a building and occupancy permit for a mobile, manufactured, or pre-owned manufactured home to be located in the city shall apply for a letter of intent from the city clerk. This letter of intent will be presented by the applicant to the county building inspector or his authorized agent before any such mobile, manufactured, or pre-owned manufactured home is located within the corporate limits of the city. The county building inspector shall issue the building and occupancy permit once he is satisfied that all requirements of this article have been complied with.
(b) A building permit is also required if the mobile, manufactured, or pre-owned manufactured home is added to or structurally altered ten square feet or more.
(c) A building permit shall not be issued for a mobile, manufactured or pre-owned manufactured home containing aluminum wiring.
(d) All mobile and manufactured homes must be registered with the county tax commissioner.
(e) All mobile and/or manufactured homes must have approval of the septic system from the county health department before a permit can be issued.
(f) An application for a building and occupancy permit for a mobile or manufactured home must be filed by the owner or owner's agent, along with a letter of intent from the city clerk, with the county building inspector. The application must contain:
(1) A description of the mobile or manufactured home as to size and dimension; year and model of the unit; the zoning district and classification; tax map and parcel number of the planned location of the mobile or manufactured home; the intended use of the mobile or manufactured home; the name of the owner and the name of the intended occupant; the source of water; and the type of waste disposal system;
(2) If the intended use of the mobile or manufactured home is as an accessory use, hardship use or farm caretaker, then details of such proposed use shall be provided by the applicant;
(3) If the application is for relocation of a mobile home which was not constructed in accordance with the federal manufactured home construction safety standards required by the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD), a pre-permitting inspection must be accomplished before a building and occupancy permit is issued;
(4) The applicant must provide a copy of a plat recorded in the office of the clerk of the superior court of the county of the tract where the mobile or manufactured home will be located and a sketch plan of where on the tract the structure itself, the components of the septic system, and the drive and parking areas are to be located;
(5) A septic tank permit from the county board of health or a verification letter for existing systems;
(6) An access letter from the state department of transportation for all new driveways accessing from a state highway;
(7) The name of the person setting up the home;
(8) The name of the electrician performing the electrical work; and
(9) Proof of a current county tax decal.
(g) Prior to obtaining a building permit it shall be unlawful to move, locate, relocate, erect or make utility connections of any kind to a mobile, manufactured, or pre-owned manufactured home within the city.
(h) Prior to obtaining a building permit it shall be unlawful to occupy or otherwise use as a residence a mobile, manufactured, or pre-owned manufactured home within the city.
(Ord. of 1-5-2015, § 4)

